title: neural_grandmother
---
<<present_speaker "npc_neural_grandmother_cell">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "neural_grandmother_met") == "satisfied">>
    Grandmother: There you are again! Every time, I light right up.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "neural_grandmother_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "neural_grandmother_met" true>>
    Grandmother: There you are! Come here, let me look at you.
    Grandmother: You've grown. You've grown antennae. No matter. It's you.
    -> I think you have me confused with someone.
        Grandmother: Nonsense. I'm a grandmother cell. I fire for one face in the whole world, and I'm firing.
        Grandmother: Look at me. All lit up.
    -> Where am I?
        Grandmother: The Callosum, dear. The bridge between the two halves. The living half is west, where I grew.
        Grandmother: The east half was built. They're nice enough over there. They learn from examples. I learned from you.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: neural_hebb
---
<<present_speaker "npc_neural_hebb">>
<<if verdict("world.flag_set", "neural_hebb_met") == "satisfied">>
    Donna: Every time you walk past, I think of that lamp. It worked.
    -> ‹go›
<<elseif verdict("world.flag_set", "neural_hebb_met") == "not_satisfied">>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "neural_hebb_met" true>>
    Donna: Hold still. You and that bulb just lit up at the same moment.
    Donna: There. Wired. Now one of you comes along whenever the other one fires.
    -> What do you do here?
        Donna: I introduce cells that fire at the same time. After that, when one fires, the other comes along.
        Donna: I need to try it a few more times with that lamp. I'm going to write down how much the response changes.
    -> What are the purple clouds?
        Donna: Intrusive thoughts. They keep turning up when I'm trying to work. I was halfway through testing a new connection when one of them knocked the bulb off the stand.
    -> ‹go›
<<else>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===
title: neural_perceptron
---
<<present_speaker "npc_neural_perceptron">>
Percy: QUESTION?
-> Are you a machine?
    Percy: YES.
-> Is exactly one of these true: the lamp is on, or the door is open?
    Percy: ...
    Percy: LAMP ON, DOOR CLOSED: YES. LAMP OFF, DOOR OPEN: YES.
    Percy: ...
    Percy: I cannot classify all four cases with one straight line. Please submit a different question.
-> Who made you?
    Percy: A man with a camera and a board of wires, in nineteen fifty-eight. The papers said I would walk and talk one day.
    Percy: I do not walk.
-> ‹go›
===
title: neural_echo
---
<<present_speaker "npc_neural_echo">>
Echo: Welcome to the Echo Chamber! Say anything.
-> The weather's nice.
    Echo: The weather's nice!
    Echo: Everyone agrees. Look at the screens. They're all saying it.
-> I think you're wrong.
    Echo: You think I'm wrong!
    Echo: So true. We all think I'm wrong. Isn't it wonderful to agree?
-> ‹say nothing›
    Echo: ...
    Echo: Silence! So brave. In here, we love silence.
-> ‹go›
===
